SCREEN:
SELECT
   ds.name          AS SCREEN_NAME,
   de.sqlname_c     AS ENTITY,
   dp.name          AS PANEL,
   den.denom        As PANEL_DENOM,
   da.sqlname_c     AS ATTRIBUTE,
   dpv.name         AS NATURE,
   dp.edit_e        AS EDITABLE,
   dp.mandatory_f   AS MANDATORY,
   dp2.name         AS PARENT_PANEL,
   den2.denom        As PANEL_DENOM
FROM dict_screen ds
INNER JOIN dict_entity de
   ON de.dict_id = ds.entity_dict_id
INNER JOIN dict_panel dp
   ON dp.screen_dict_id = ds.dict_id
LEFT JOIN dict_attribute da
   ON da.dict_id = dp.attribute_dict_id
LEFT JOIN dict_panel dp2
   ON dp2.dict_id = dp.parent_panel_dict_id
LEFT JOIN dict_entity de_panel
   ON de_panel.sqlname_c = 'dict_panel'
LEFT JOIN dict_attribute da_nature
   ON da_nature.entity_dict_id = de_panel.dict_id
  AND da_nature.sqlname_c = 'nature_e'
INNER JOIN dict_perm_value dpv
   ON dpv.attribute_dict_id = da_nature.dict_id
  AND dpv.perm_val_nat_e = dp.nature_e
LEFT JOIN denomination den 
   ON dp.dict_id = den.object_id
LEFT JOIN denomination den2
   ON dp.parent_panel_dict_id = den2.object_id
ORDER BY
   ds.name,
   de.sqlname_c,
   dp.name,
   da.sqlname_c;
 
Drilldown 1
User clicks the PROFILE_CODE corresponds to PROFILE_TYPE = SCREEN
This will return the output of SCREEN_PROFILE query - Composition of all Screens.
 
DrillDown 2 - 
On the drilldown output, User clicks any items on the SCREEN_NAME column. 
This will populate the output from the query 2 (SCREEN). 
 
